#HELPS

0 CLASSHELPERS~
Additional legacy class commands are implemented in more.c.
Use HELP followed by the command for its syntax and native requirements.
These include Vampire discipline forms, blood/illusion controls,
Necromancy corpse powers, Spirit Guardian and Celerity.
Help access does not grant a class, discipline or execution permission.
Presence of a help entry is not exhaustive effect/variant certification.
~

0 MINDBLAST~
Syntax: mindblast <target>
Vampire, Auspex 7. Makes the native mind-blast attack against a visible
room target, subject to combat safety; it cannot target the caster.
This is an attack, not a guaranteed stun or staff slay.
~

0 MALLEABLE CHANGELING~
Syntax: malleable <NPC>
        malleable self
Vampire, Vicissitude 1. Copies a local NPC's appearance using the native
malleable/disguise form. SELF restores an active malleable appearance.
Other polymorphs and Zulo Form can prevent the change.
~

0 FLESHCRAFT~
Syntax: fleshcraft
Vampire, Vicissitude 2. Toggles the native protective flesh-soak craft.
It is a body-craft setting, not a permanent increase to trained statistics.
~

0 BONECRAFT~
Syntax: bonecraft talons
        bonecraft quills
        bonecraft <target>
Vampire, Vicissitude 3. TALONS and QUILLS toggle their body crafts.
Warning: each toggle hurts the caster for 5% of maximum health for talons,
or 50% for quills, including when removing the craft. Do not toggle at low HP.
The targeted bone-crafting attack currently requires an existing fight
and a local target; it uses native combat safety.
~

0 ZULOFORM~
Syntax: zuloform
Vampire, Vicissitude 5. Toggles the native huge-monster polymorph.
Incompatible existing forms can block it. Repeat the command to revert.
~

0 PLASMAFORM~
Syntax: plasmaform
Vampire, Vicissitude 4. Uses the native spilt-blood object-body form.
A fight timer and incompatible polymorph prevent activation. The form
handles its native restraints/web/tendril release and return path.
This is not the same power as Shadow Body or Spirit Form.
~

0 CONDITIONING~
Syntax: conditioning <player>
Vampire, Dominate 2. Attempts native player conditioning/loyalty.
Both participants must meet the native PK requirements. It cannot be
used on the caster or NPCs. Eye contact and willpower/resistance apply;
Dominate 6 changes the native failed-eye-contact gate.
It does not change a character's clan or staff rank.
~

0 TONGUE~
Syntax: tongue <target>
        tongue <carried weapon>
Vampire, Serpentis 2. Uses Tongue of the Serpent against a room target,
or poisons an eligible carried weapon. In combat, omitting the target
uses the current opponent. Not every weapon can receive the poison.
~

0 MUMMIFY~
Syntax: mummify
Vampire, Serpentis 3. Enters or leaves the native mummified corpse-body
mode. Incompatible polymorphs prevent activation. The corpse representation
does not mean the caster has permanently died.
~

0 CONTROLBEAST~
Syntax: controlbeast
        controlbeast buy
Vampire beast-control training. The first form displays the current offer;
BUY spends (100 - truebeast) primal and reduces truebeast by one.
Active frenzy, complete loss of control, existing Golconda and prior
diablerie can prevent the purchase. It is not a free frenzy toggle.
~

0 SHROUDNIGHT~
Syntax: shroudnight
Vampire Obtenebration 1, or Werewolf Uktena 1.
Calls room darkness and records ownership of that darkness on the caster.
Repeat to dismiss your active shroud. An already-dark room cannot simply
be claimed by a second caster.
~

0 SILENCEDEATH SILENCEOFDEATH~
Syntax: silencedeath
Vampire, Quietus 1. Calls the native room-silence effect and records its
owner. Repeat to dismiss your active silence. Existing room silence
cannot simply be claimed by another caster.
~

0 WEAKNESS~
Syntax: weakness <target>
Vampire, Quietus 2. Applies the native strength-reducing curse to a local
eligible target. This is not permanent stat training removal.
~

0 INFIRMITY~
Syntax: infirmity <target>
Vampire, Quietus 3. Applies native infirmity ability penalties to a local
eligible target. Its affects use the existing spell/affect system.
~

0 BLOODAGONY~
Syntax: bloodagony <carried weapon>
Vampire, Quietus 4. Spends 10 current blood to mark an eligible weapon
for native aggravated damage. Already-marked weapons, artifacts, relics
and switched-body objects cannot receive the treatment.
~

0 SPIT TASTEDEATH~
Syntax: spit <target>
Vampire, Quietus 5. Uses the native Taste of Death attack.
Omitting the target during combat uses the current opponent.
~

0 SHADOWBODY~
Syntax: shadowbody
Vampire, Obtenebration 3. Toggles the native shadow/ethereal body.
A fight timer or incompatible polymorph can block it; native restraint
release applies on activation. This is not Tenebrous Form.
~

0 ARMSABYSS~
Syntax: armsabyss <target>
Vampire, Obtenebration 2. Uses native shadow tendrils on a local target,
or the current opponent when omitted in combat. It can remove existing
native tendrils as well as apply them; ethereal targets cannot be bound.
~

0 LAMPREY~
Syntax: lamprey <target>
Vampire, Obtenebration 4. Calls the native damaging, blood-draining
lamprey/tendrils effect on a room target. Omitting the target in combat
uses the current opponent. The caster's blood pool still caps the gain.
~

0 THANATOPSIS~
Syntax: thanatopsis <corpse>
Vampire, Necromancy 1. Examines the corpse's recorded killer information.
The corpse must be accessible, and missing records can prevent discovery.
It does not reveal arbitrary account details or a living player's inventory.
~

0 SPIRITGATE~
Syntax: spiritgate <NPC corpse>
Vampire, Necromancy 3. Uses the corpse's recorded destination to create
temporary paired spirit portals. Player corpses and invalid/same-room
destinations cannot be used. The corpse and native portal mechanics apply;
this is not the Mage RIFT command or a player-unlocked GATE spell.
~

0 PRESERVE PRESERVATION~
Syntax: preserve <corpse>
Vampire, Necromancy 2. Preserves an eligible corpse through the native
corpse handler. Already-preserved, incompatible or unsupported objects
are rejected. It does not animate the corpse.
~

0 ZOMBIE~
Syntax: zombie <NPC corpse>
Vampire, Necromancy 5. Animates an eligible NPC corpse lying in the room.
Drop carried corpses first. The native Necromancy reuse timer, original
mobile data and available templates constrain animation.
~

0 SPIRITFORM~
Syntax: spiritform
Vampire, Protean 5. Toggles the native flying, ethereal spirit polymorph.
Incompatible forms can prevent changing; native restraint release applies.
Spirit Form does not automatically grant unrestricted teleportation.
~

0 SPIRITGUARDIAN SPIRITFRIEND~
Syntax: spiritguardian
Native requirements: Vampire Necromancy 4, Werewolf Children of Gaia 4,
or Monk Mantra 6. Calls or dismisses the MORE_GUARDIAN protection.
It is a protective spirit state with native guardian messages, not a
spawned fighting follower. It does not grant staff immunity.
~

0 SUCCULENCE~
Syntax: succulence <NPC>
Vampire, Animalism 5. Improves an NPC's blood by doubling its native
current blood and blood-pool values once. Already-improved creatures,
players and the caster cannot be treated.
~

0 FRENZYTRIGGER~
Syntax: frenzytrigger
Vampire, Animalism 6. Toggles the native inner-beast frenzy and associated
fangs, and available Protean claws/nightsight. Repeating it forces the
beast back. This differs from the restored FRENZY spell's modest buff.
~

0 SHADOWPLAY~
Syntax: shadowplay
Vampire, Obtenebration 1. Hides the caster using the native shadow effect.
Outdoor sunlight and already being hidden prevent activation.
~

0 SHADOWSTEP STEP~
Syntax: shadowstep <target>
Vampire, Obtenebration 5. Travels to a valid, standing world target.
Player targets require native summoning consent. Safe/private/solitary
destinations, own familiars, illusions and unsuitable targets are rejected.
Both-room no-recall/no-teleport/private/solitary protection, combat timers,
restraints/root/curse/web, switched bodies and incompatible planes block it.
It retains its native no-mana fee; it is not Werewolf Bridge Walk or RIFT.
~

0 SPIRITEYES~
Syntax: spiriteyes
Vampire, Necromancy 1. Toggles native Spirit Eyes and shadowsight.
This is perception into the shadowlands, not movement into them.
~

0 SBREATH~
Syntax: sbreath
Vampire, Serpentis 5. Makes native Basilisk breath attacks against eligible
other room occupants, using the existing combat-safety checks.
It is an area attack, not a single target command or guaranteed poison.
~

0 CELERITY~
Syntax: celerity
        celerity renew
Vampire, Celerity 1 or higher. Activation spends 10 current blood and
adds 50 to the native Celerity duration; the existing duration cap applies.
RENEW toggles automatic combat renewal. This is not ordinary stance
training or the Werewolf's differently implemented speed gifts.
~

0 CHIROPTEAN~
Syntax: chiroptean
Vampire, Vicissitude 6. Toggles the native Chiroptean Marauder bat form.
Incompatible polymorphs can prevent the change; repeat to return.
~

0 EMPATHY~
Syntax: empathy <target>
Vampire, Presence 7. Removes the target's native Conditioning loyalty
flag if present. It does not train an empathy statistic.
This is distinct from the reconstructed Werewolf MASKEMPATHY gift.
~

0 $~
